 numerous bugs and reduced memory usage by ~80MB on startup for large repositories.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-03-19\",\n    \"community_feedback\": [\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"#ClaudeCode is all you need in 2026. Claude Code in 2026 is not what it was when it launched. After a year of building frameworks, custom tools, and more\",\n        \"source\": \"X/Twitter\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Hooks let you run code automatically before or after Claude makes changes. Running Prettier on every file Claude touches\",\n        \"source\": \"X/Twitter\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"⚠️ Important warning: If you Google 'install Claude Code,' the top result is malware. Attackers are buying Google Ads for fake Claude Code installers\",\n        \"source\": \"X/Twitter\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    \"title\": \"Version 2.1.79 Release\",\n    \"description\": \"Added --console flag for Anthropic Console authentication, Show turn duration toggle, and VSCode remote-control feature. Fixed numerous issues including subprocess hanging, Ctrl+C in print mode, voice mode activation, and improved startup memory usage by ~18MB.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-03-19\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    \"title\": \"Persistent Agent Thread Feature (Mobile/Desktop Control)\",\n    \"description\": \"Pro and Max plan users can access a persistent agent thread via Claude Desktop or Claude for iOS/Android to manage tasks in Cowork, extending Claude Code's agentic capabilities to mobile devices.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    \"url\": \"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-03-17\",\n    \"community_feedback\": [\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Reports of code's death are greatly exaggerated - Chris Lattner reviewed a compiler written entirely by Claude AI\",\n        \"source\": \"HackerNews\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    \"title\": \"Voice Mode, Session Forking, and Remote Control\",\n    \"description\": \"Major March 2026 updates bringing Voice Mode with 20-language support and push-to-talk functionality, session forking for isolated sub-agent execution, remote sessions with session teleportation between devices, enhanced transcript search, improved sandbox controls, and customizable keybindings.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    \"url\": \"https://buungroup.com/blog/claude-code-new-features-2026\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-03-15\",\n    \"community_feedback\": [\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Claude Code and the Great Productivity Panic of 2026 - spending time working with Claude Code leaves me feeling the same way I feel after a day scrolling Reddit and HN - a thin, jittery, frayed...\",\n        \"source\": \"HackerNews\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Since Claude Code + Claude 4.0 were released, the entire vibe changed... 99.9% of engineers think that coding (even engineering) [is solved]\",\n        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Voice mode is rolling out now in Claude Code. It's live for ~5% of users today\",\n        \"source\": \"X/Twitter\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"AI increased completion time by 19% vs. predicted 24% savings - wild perception gaps from DeveloperWeek 2026\",\n        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      },\n      {\n        